<title>USA: Snap-on Iowa workers ratify contract.</title>
<headline>Snap-on Iowa workers ratify contract.</headline>
<dateline>KENOSHA, Wis. 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Snap-on Inc said Tuesday that union membership at its Algona, Iowa manufacturing plant ratified a new three-year agreement with the company.</p>
<p>The contract, ratified on April 12, covers about 340 employees represented by Lodge 1045 of the International Association of Machinists and Aerospace Workers.</p>
<p>The Algona plant produces tool storage units for professional auto technicians and industrial customers.</p>
<p>Snap-on manufactures tools and equipment.</p>
<p>	   ((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
